═══════════════════════════════════════════

FEATURES:
1. Earbud Mode (Continuous Bidirectional Translation):
   - User wears earbuds, speaks Language A → Nova translates to Language B → TTS plays in earbud.
   - Other person speaks Language B → Nova translates to Language A → TTS plays in earbud.
   - Latency target: <800ms end-to-end using streaming Whisper + Gemini Translate + Streaming TTS.

2. Camera Overlay Translation (AR Enhanced):
   - Point camera at foreign menu/sign → Real-time OCR → Translate → Render translated text OVER original text preserving font/style/color (inpainting technique).
   - Uses ML Kit Text Recognition + Gemini Translation + Canvas inpainting.

3. Conversation Mode (Group Chat):
   - 3+ people speaking different languages around phone.
   - Nova identifies speaker by voice profile (from Phase 5 biometrics).
   - Translates each utterance to all other listeners' preferred languages simultaneously.
   - Displays color-coded transcript in chat: [Ali (Urdu)]: "Hello" → [Translated to English for John]: "Hello"

IMPLEMENTATION:
```kotlin
object UniversalTranslator {
    private var sourceLang = "auto"
    private var targetLang = "en"
    private var isEarbudModeActive = false
    
    fun startEarbudMode(source: String, target: String) {
        sourceLang = source
        targetLang = target
        isEarbudModeActive = true
        
        // Start continuous STT loop
        ContinuousSpeechRecognizer.start { transcript, detectedLang ->
            if(detectedLang == source) {
                // Translate and speak in target language
                lifecycleScope.launch {
                    val translated = translateText(transcript, source, target)
                    TextToSpeechEngine.speak(translated, languageCode = target)
                    
                    // Send transcript to paired earbud/device if applicable
                    MeshNetwork.broadcast(JSONObject()
                        .put("type", "translation_stream")
                        .put("original", transcript)
                        .put("translated", translated))
                }
            }
        }
    }
    
    suspend fun translateText(text: String, from: String, to: String): String {
        // Use Gemini for high-quality contextual translation
        val prompt = "Translate the following text from $from to $to. Preserve tone and idioms. Text: \"$text\""
        return LlmManager.ask(prompt, "You are a professional translator.")
    }
    
    fun renderArTranslation(bitmap: Bitmap, detectedTextBlocks: List<TextBlock>): Bitmap {
        val canvas = Canvas(bitmap.copy(Bitmap.Config.ARGB_8888, true))
        
        detectedTextBlocks.forEach { block ->
            val originalText = block.text
            val translatedText = runBlocking { translateText(originalText, "auto", Locale.getDefault().language) }
            
            // Clear original text region (simple rectangle fill with surrounding color)
            val bgColor = sampleBackgroundColor(bitmap, block.boundingBox)
            canvas.drawRect(block.boundingBox, Paint().apply { color = bgColor })
            
            // Draw translated text with matched font size/style
            val textSize = calculateFontSize(block.boundingBox.height(), translatedText.length)
            canvas.drawText(translatedText, block.boundingBox.left.toFloat(), 
                           block.boundingBox.bottom.toFloat(), 
                           Paint().apply { 
                               this.textSize = textSize
                               this.color = Color.BLACK
                               this.typeface = Typeface.DEFAULT_BOLD
                           })
        }
        
        return canvas.bitmap
    }
}
```

